#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "&i18n-kapplication; is a chat application that lets you talk with AI language models, either running locally with Ollama or provided by an online AI service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Conversations are stored in a local database on your computer, so they are still there the next time you start the application. You can browse them, search through them, organize them in projects and with tags, archive the ones you do not need any more, and export them to a file. When you do not want a conversation to be kept at all, you can use an ephemeral discussion instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "&i18n-kapplication; does not provide a model of its own: it talks to a model provider that you configure. Nothing is sent anywhere until you have set up such a provider and asked a question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before you can ask anything, &i18n-kapplication; needs at least one <emphasis>instance</emphasis>. An instance is a configured connection to a model provider: a local server running on your own machine, or an online service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "The first time you start the application without any instance, it offers to create one. You can also open <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and go to the <guilabel>Instances</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a local model"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "Running the model on your own computer keeps your questions on your machine. &i18n-kapplication; can use local servers such as <application>Ollama</application>, <application>llama.cpp</application> or <application>LM Studio</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Install and start the server first, then add an instance of the matching type. The default address of a local <application>Ollama</application> server is already filled in. If <application>Ollama</application> is installed but not running, &i18n-kapplication; offers to start it for you; you can also do this from the command line with <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--start-ollama</option></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once the instance is connected you still need a model. Models can be downloaded from within the instance configuration, and &i18n-kapplication; notifies you when a download is finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using an online service"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "&i18n-kapplication; can also talk to hosted services, among them Ollama Cloud, OpenAI, Anthropic, Mistral AI, Groq, Grok, Qwen, OpenRouter, DeepInfra, Novita AI, Cerebras and other providers with an OpenAI-compatible interface. The exact list depends on the plugins installed on your system; run <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--plugin-info</option></userinput> to see it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create an instance of the matching type and paste the API key given to you by the service. Be aware that with an online service your questions, and any file you attach, are sent to that provider and are subject to its own privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &i18n-kapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "The window is split in three parts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "the list of your chats, on the left. It can be collapsed with the button on the splitter;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "the conversation itself, on the right, where your questions and the answers of the model are shown;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "the input field at the bottom, where you type your question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Above them, a header bar lets you start a new chat or an ephemeral discussion, mark the current chat as a favorite and search in the current conversation. The status bar at the bottom shows what the model is currently doing, for instance which tool it is calling."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Asking questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type your question in the input field and validate it. The answer appears in the conversation view as it is being generated, and a notification is shown when a long answer is finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can attach files to a question, and enable the tools the model is allowed to call while answering it, including the ones provided by your MCP servers (see <xref linkend=\"mcp-servers\"/>). Each chat keeps its own history, which is sent along with your new question so that the model knows the context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can attach files to a question, and enable the tools the model is allowed to call while answering it. Each chat keeps its own history, which is sent along with your new question so that the model knows the context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing chats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Chats are created from the header bar, or with <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--new-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right-click a chat in the list to act on it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modify…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the title of the chat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Duplicate…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a copy of the chat, for instance to try another direction without losing the original conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set as Favorite"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show the chat in the <guilabel>Favorite</guilabel> section at the top of the list. The same can be done with the <guibutton>Favorite</guibutton> button of the header bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the chat into a project, or out of it with <guimenuitem>No Project</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add tags to the chat or remove them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Archive"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide the chat from the list without deleting it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the chat and its messages for good."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "The other chats are grouped by age: today, the last seven days, the last thirty days and older."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "A conversation can also be forked from one of its messages with the <guibutton>Fork</guibutton> button shown next to it. This starts a new chat containing the conversation up to that message, and leaves the original chat untouched."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "A chat you do not need any more can be archived instead of being deleted. Archived chats are hidden from the list; show them again with <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Archive</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "To look for something you asked or read some time ago, use <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Search in Database…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This searches the whole stored history, not only the chat you are looking at. The number of matches is shown in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Projects and tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Projects and tags are two ways of organizing your chats. A chat belongs to at most one project, which is useful to keep together the conversations about the same piece of work. A chat can have any number of tags."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Both are created, renamed and removed with <guimenuitem>Manage Projects…</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Manage Tags…</guimenuitem>, in the <guisubmenu>Project</guisubmenu> and <guisubmenu>Tags</guisubmenu> submenus of the context menu of the chat list. Removing a project does not remove its chats: they are kept, outside of any project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tag selector above the chat list only shows the chats which have one of the selected tags. Select no tag to see all of them again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ephemeral discussions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "An ephemeral discussion is a chat which is never written to the database. Use it for a question you do not want to keep: once you close &i18n-kapplication;, it is gone. Start one with the <guibutton>Ephemeral Discussion</guibutton> button of the header bar, or with <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--ephemeral-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable></userinput>. Ephemeral discussions are shown in their own section at the top of the chat list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you change your mind, the <guibutton>Save Discussion in Database</guibutton> button of the header bar turns it into a normal chat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep in mind that this only concerns what is stored on your computer: with an online service, your questions are still sent to that provider."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Ask"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Ask is a small dialog for a single question, without opening the main window. Open it with <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open Quick Ask…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, with the <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Meta;<keycap>Space</keycap></keycombo> global shortcut, or with <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--quick-ask</option></userinput>. Questions asked this way are not added to your chats, unless you keep the discussion with the <guibutton>Save Discussion in Database</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing and exporting chats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current chat can be saved to a file with <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, in one of four formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as JSON…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <filename class=\"extension\">.kaichat</filename> file. This is the only format that &i18n-kapplication; can read back."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Markdown…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "A text file keeping the formatting of the answers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Text…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plain text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Pdf…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "A printable document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "A previously exported <filename class=\"extension\">.kaichat</filename> file is read back with <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. You can also open such a file from your file manager, or pass it on the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjusting the display"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "The text of the whole application can be made bigger or smaller with <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Font Size</guisubmenu></menuchoice>, or with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> and <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo>. A fixed font can be chosen in the configuration dialog instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Color Scheme</guisubmenu></menuchoice> switches the colors of the window without changing your desktop settings, and <keycap>F11</keycap> switches to full screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "The menu bar can be hidden with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Menubar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>; the actions stay available through the hamburger button of the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &i18n-kapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "The configuration dialog is opened with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Depending on how the application was built, it has the following pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether the system tray icon is shown, and the system prompt sent to the model at the beginning of every conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use a font of your choice instead of the system one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Instances"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add, remove and configure the connections to your model providers, and manage the models available on them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "MCP Servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Model Context Protocol servers, which give the model access to external data and actions. See <xref linkend=\"mcp-servers\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Model Context Protocol servers, which give the model access to external data and actions. This support is still experimental."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spell Checking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spell checking of what you type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text-to-speech settings, when the application was built with text-to-speech support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable or disable the installed plugins and configure the tools the model may use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Feedback"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "How much information, if any, you want to send to the developers. Nothing is sent unless you ask for it here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "Retention"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "How long your chats are kept. <guilabel>Retention Days</guilabel> is the number of days after which old chats are removed; with the default value of 0, they are kept for ever. <guilabel>Exclude Favorite Chats</guilabel>, enabled by default, keeps your favorite chats whatever their age."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows where your chats are stored on disk. The path can be copied to the clipboard with the button next to it, for instance to back up or delete the database."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notifications are configured with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Notifications…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Instances and MCP servers can also be configured outside of the application, from the <guilabel>AI</guilabel> module of &systemsettings;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "MCP servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard which lets a model use tools provided by external programs, called MCP servers: reading your files, querying a database, searching a documentation, and so on. &i18n-kapplication; acts as an MCP client: it connects to the servers you configure and offers their tools to the model."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid "Servers are managed on the <guilabel>MCP Servers</guilabel> page of the configuration dialog. Use the <guibutton>Add Server…</guibutton> button, or the context menu of the list, to add one; double-click a server or use <guimenuitem>Edit…</guimenuitem> to modify it, and <guimenuitem>Remove Server</guimenuitem> to delete it. The checkbox in front of each server enables or disables it without losing its configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each server has a <guilabel>Name</guilabel>, an optional <guilabel>Icon</guilabel> and a <guilabel>Type</guilabel>, which tells how &i18n-kapplication; talks to it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Standard IO"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "The server is a program started by &i18n-kapplication; on your computer. Enter the <guilabel>Command</guilabel> to run and its <guilabel>Arguments</guilabel>, as given in the documentation of the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "Streamable HTTP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "The server is reached over the network at the given <guilabel>URL</guilabel>. Additional <guilabel>Headers</guilabel>, for instance an <literal>Authorization</literal> header holding an access token, can be added in <quote>Name: Value</quote> form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>SSE</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "The older HTTP transport based on Server-Sent Events, still used by some servers. Enter its <guilabel>URL</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Allowed folders</guilabel> lists the folders the server may work in. The list is passed to the server, which is expected to restrict itself to these folders; a server which accesses files usually needs at least one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changes are applied when you close the configuration dialog with <guibutton>OK</guibutton> or <guibutton>Apply</guibutton>. MCP servers can also be configured from the <guilabel>AI</guilabel> module of &systemsettings;; the list is shared with the other applications using it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using MCP tools in a chat"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "Every enabled server is shown as a button among the tools available under the input field. Check the button to let the model use the tools of this server for your next questions. The arrow next to it opens a menu listing these tools, from which you can select only some of them; &i18n-kapplication; connects to the server the first time this menu is opened, in order to know its tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "While the model is calling a tool, its name is shown in the status bar, and the result is sent back to the model to complete its answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "Confirmations and requests"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid "A tool can do more than read data, so &i18n-kapplication; asks before running one. The <guilabel>Run Tool</guilabel> dialog shows the server, the tool and the arguments the model wants to pass to it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run the tool this time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always Allow This Server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run the tool, and no longer ask for any tool of this server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deny"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do not run the tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "The servers whose tools run without confirmation are checked in the <guilabel>Run tools without confirmation</guilabel> list of the <guilabel>MCP Servers</guilabel> page, where you can uncheck them again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "A server can also ask something of you or of the model while it works:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "it can ask you to fill in some information, in a <guilabel>Request from</guilabel> dialog showing the fields it needs. <guibutton>Accept</guibutton> sends your answer, <guibutton>Decline</guibutton> refuses to give it;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid "it can ask the model to generate some text for it. The <guilabel>Sampling Request from MCP Server</guilabel> dialog shows what would be sent to the model; nothing is sent unless you choose <guibutton>Send to LLM</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only add servers you trust. A <guilabel>Standard IO</guilabel> server is a program running with your own rights, and what a tool returns is read by the model and, with an online service, sent to its provider along with your conversation."
msgstr ""

